/-!
# Fusion and factor alignment in 13.9.9–10

These exports prove the transfer reduction to the two marked involution
classes, the weak-closure contradiction for the literal `B ∩ Q`, and the
construction of the terminal involution in `M₁ \ O²(M₁)` once `Δ₃` is
fused to `z`.

The marked orbit computations, the actual minus orthogonal module
recognition, and the `R₁ × R₂` factor comparison and witness construction
remain necessary. Thus these conditional reductions do not yet establish
all clauses of source 13.9.9 or 13.9.10.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
printed pp.972–974 (PDF pp.989–991).
-/
